2026-08-29  stevensko <skovraneksteven@gmail.com>

	* Fork of vcsh, rebranded as "Stache Dotfiles Manager"
	* Command renamed vcsh -> stache
	* Environment variables renamed VCSH_* -> STACHE_*
	* Nothing is created under $HOME any more. Everything lives in
	  $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/stache/:
	    - one <repo>.stache/ directory per repo, containing:
	        <repo>.git/     the git directory
	        config          per-repo shell config (sourced), was config.d/<repo>
	        .gitignore      per-repo ignore file  (was ~/.gitignore.d/<repo>)
	        .gitattributes  per-repo attributes   (was ~/.gitattributes.d/<repo>)
	    - shared fallbacks .gitignore / .gitattributes / .gitconfig, the
	      stache.repos list, and the hooks/ overlays/ config dirs/files
	  upgrade() points core.excludesfile / core.attributesfile at the
	  per-repo file if present, else the shared one. These files are no
	  longer tracked by the repo (they are outside $HOME).
	* The shared .gitignore is seeded with `*` on first run, so `git add .`
	  in a stache repo is safe by default; `stache <repo> add -f <path>`
	  tracks a new file. Trade-off: `stache list-untracked` returns nothing
	  unless you make a curated per-repo .gitignore (stache write-gitignore).
	* Hook/overlay dirs lost the -enabled suffix: hooks/ and overlays/.
	* System config: /etc/vcsh/config -> /etc/stache/config
	* Source script renamed vcsh.in -> stache.in; man page vcsh.1 -> stache.1
	* $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/stache/stache.repos ("<name> <url> <branch>" per repo
	  with an origin remote) is created and kept current AUTOMATICALLY after
	  init/clone/delete/rename/upgrade/bootstrap. There is no `manifest`
	  command. `stache bootstrap` -- equivalently `stache clone --all` or
	  `stache clone -a` -- clones everything listed there that is not already
	  present. Built-in, no myrepos/gita.
	* New: `stache config <git config args>` edits a shared git config file
	  ($STACHE_GITCONFIG) that every repo includes via include.path;
	  set credential.helper, user.email, etc. once for all repos
	* upgrade now sets status.showUntrackedFiles (default no, override with
	  $STACHE_SHOW_UNTRACKED) so `git status` in a repo ignores $HOME
	* delete: use `git ls-files -z | xargs -0` so paths with whitespace,
	  glob characters, or non-ASCII bytes are removed correctly
	* Drop the myrepos (post-init-setup-mr) sample hook; bootstrapping is
	  now built in (see the stache.repos / bootstrap notes above)
	* Add install-local.sh for a no-autotools user-space install

